            of the core inclusion with itself:
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1 \coloneqq (i_C/i_C)
          %p
            This exposition is further developed in
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#Segal%20space#ConstructionFromACategory"} Segal space – construction from a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            a homotopy-theoretic kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            which is now not a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            anymore (a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            is, but which is now a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} simplicial object in an (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ↪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hookrightarrow
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
            it contains not the
            %em set
            of sequences of composable morphisms, but the “space” of such sequences, which just as the “space”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0
            of objects knows all the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies"} homotopies
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalences"} equivalences
            between such sequences of composable morphisms.
          %p
            One then recalls a basic fact of traditional
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            precisely if it satisfies the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+conditions"} Segal conditions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+products"} fiber products
            of the 1-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplices"} simplices
            over the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertices"} vertices
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
            is built in degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            by a
            = succeed "-fold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+product"} homotopy fiber product
            of the space of 1-simplices over the space of vertices, and indeed one finds that it is.
          %p
            In traditional category theory a simplicial set is the nerve of a category if and only if it satisfies the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+conditions"} Segal conditions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi core
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_C \colon core(C) \to C
            we could have started with
            %em any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon K \to C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi i
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n \coloneqq i^{/^n}
            would still defined a simplicial groupoid that satisfies the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+conditions"} Segal conditions
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+product"} homotopy fiber product
            = succeed "-inclusion" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Segal+space"} compleness
            condition”, and more recently also called a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence"} univalence
            condition).
          %p
            Finally, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            of a category in fact contains lots of redundant information. It is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coskeleton"} 2-coskeletal
            and hence in a precise sense already its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeleton"} 2-skeleton
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 2
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_2 \stackrel{\to}{\stackrel{\to}{\to}} X_1 \stackrel{\to}{\to} X_0
            contains all the relevant information. Therefore we may decide to write this out explicitly in terms of a further
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} dependent type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_2
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compositions"} compositions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%281%2C1%29-categories"} (1,1)-categories
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            is spelled out below in
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#1CategoryTypes"} (1,1)-Category types
          %p
            But of course the point of category objects internal to an
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} simplicial objects in an (∞,1)-category
            and the appropriate conditions on them to qualify as internal categories. The comprehensive discussion of this definition we turn to in
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#Definition"} Definition
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            We define category objects internal to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            (and with respect to a choice of “inclusion of groupoids”
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}\hookrightarrow \mathcal{C}
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} co
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} reflective sub-(∞,1)-categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi Cat
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi PreCat
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{H}
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  Cat_{\mathbf{H}}(\mathcal{C})
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  PreCat_{\mathbf{H}}(\mathcal{C})
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  \\mathcal{C}^{\Delta^{op}}
          %p of that of
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#SimplicialObjects"}> Simplicial objects in an (∞,1)-category
              \.
          %p
            The definition makes recourse to the notion of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} groupoid object in an (∞,1)-category
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#GroupoidObjects"}> Groupoid objects in an (∞,1)-category
              \.
          %p Then we discuss the definition of
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#CategoryObjectInTopos"}> Internal categories in an (∞,1)-topos
              \.
          %p
            The canonical example here is the archtypical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Segal+space"} complete Segal space
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-categories of (∞,1)-sheaves
            (of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
          %p
            More generally, given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} fully faithful inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} \hookrightarrow \mathcal{C}
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            into some other
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#InAnInfinity1Category"}> Internal categories in an (∞,1)-category
              \.
          %p
            The archetypical example here is the case where again
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo =
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} =: (\infty,0)Cat
            and where then, by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo ↪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd \hookrightarrow (\infty,n)Cat
            that of
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-categories"} (∞,n)-categories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-fold+complete+Segal+spaces"} (n+1)-fold complete Segal spaces
            = succeed "-categories." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n+1)
          %p
            But again, more generally,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            can be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            for instance an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C2%29-topos"} (∞,2)-topos
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C2%29-sheaves"} (∞,2)-sheaves
            = succeed "-sheaves," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,3)
          %h3#SimplicialObjects Simplicial objects
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} reflective sub-(∞,1)-categories
            of that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} simplicial objects in an (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta^{op}}
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %p
            We frequently refer to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/powering"} powering
            of a simplicial object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
            by a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(K)
            %em
              %a{:href => "simplicial+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category#Powering"} simplicial object in an (∞,1)-category – Powering
            \.
          #RemarkNoNeedForLocalization.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              It is noteworthy that category objects internal to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %em full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} sub-(∞,1)-category
              of that of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} simplicial objects in an (∞,1)-category
              = succeed "a" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+categories"} internal categories
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+functors"} internal functors
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graphs"} graphs
              on the internal categories needs to be further
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localized
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2C1%29-category"} (n,1)-category
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              too low.
            %p
              For a discussion of how for plain
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+categories"} internal categories
              (those that also externally are
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-categories"} 1-categories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
              (instead of just a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-topos"} 2-topos
              the section
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "2-topos#InTermsOfInternalCategories"} In terms of internal categories
          %h3#PreCategoryInTopos Pre-category objects
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limit"} finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limits"} (∞,1)-limits
          #PreCategoryObject.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              An
              %strong internal precategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} simplicial object in an (∞,1)-category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X : \Delta^{op} \to \mathcal{C}
            %p
              such that it satifies the
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+condition"} Segal condition
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              exhibits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X([n])
              as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limit"} (∞,1)-limit
              \/ iterated
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %munder
                            %mo ×
                            %mrow
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi ⋯
                          %munder
                            %mo ×
                            %mrow
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi factors
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X([n]) \simeq
                    \\underbrace{
                    X(\{0,1\}) \underset{X([0])}{\times} \cdots \underset{X[0]}{\times} X(\{n-1,n\})
                    }_{n \; factors}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PreCat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PreCat(\mathcal{C})
              for the
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} full sub-(∞,1)-category
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects"} simplicial objects
              on the internal precategories.
          %p
            This is called a
            %em category object
            in (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, def. 1.1.1
            ). Here we reserve that term for those objects that behave more like category objects should, which are the
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Segal+space"} complete Segal space
                objects
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              By the discussion at
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "Segal%20condition#InTermsOfSheafConditionForSimplicialObjects"} Segal conditions – In terms of sheaf conditions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PreCat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PreCat(\mathcal{C})
              sits in an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
              square in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29Cat"} (∞,1)Cat
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi PreCat
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mi op
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Graphs
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mrow
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mn 0
                                  %mi op
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    PreCat(\mathcal{C}) &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; \mathcal{C}^{\Delta^{op}}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    Graphs(\mathcal{C})
                    \&amp;\hookrightarrow&amp;
                    \\mathcal{C}^{\Delta_0^{op}}
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 0
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_0^{op} \to \Delta
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wide+subcategory"} wide subcategory
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
              on the injective maps that moreover send elementary edges to elementary edges (morphisms of linear
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graphs"} graphs
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph"} graph
              object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∂
                            %mn 0
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∂
                            %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1 \stackrel{\overset{\partial_1}{\to}}{\underset{\partial_0}{\to}} X_0
              to the object which in degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %munder
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mn 1
                            %munder
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi X
                                  %mn 0
                            %mi ⋯
                            %munder
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi X
                                  %mn 0
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mn 1
                          %mo ⏟
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi factors
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underbrace{ X_1 \underset{X_0}{\times} \cdots \underset{X_0}{\times} X_1}_{n\; factors}
          #CompositionInPreCategory.num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+conditions"} Segal conditions
              imply that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
              a pre-category object, there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %munderover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mo ∂
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mo ∂
                          %mn 2
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∂
                          %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_1 \times_{X_0} X_1
                    \\underoverset{\simeq}{(\partial_0, \partial_2)^{-1}}{\to}
                    X_2
                    \\stackrel{\partial_1}{\to}
                    X_1
            %p
              which satisfies
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associativity
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+law"} unit law
              up to higher
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence"} coherent
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} subobject in an (∞,1)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \hookrightarrow X_1
              on such that restricted along this inclusion this composition becomes invertible we call a subobject of equivalences.
          #Equivalences.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
              a pre-category object, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PreCategoryObject"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Equiv
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Equiv(X_1) \hookrightarrow X_1
            %p
              for the maximal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} subobject in an (∞,1)-category
              of the object of 1-morphisms on those which are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalences"} equivalences
              with respect to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              of remark
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompositionInPreCategory"}
          %h3#GroupoidObjects Groupoid objects
          %p
            A
            %em groupoid object
            is a pre-category object, def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PreCategoryObject"}
            whose composition operation according to remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompositionInPreCategory"}
            is invertible. This is discussed in more detail at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} groupoid object in an (∞,1)-category
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#GroupoidObjectDefinition"} Definition
          %p and then discuss the crucial property for the further developments here, which is the
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#CoreflectionOfGroupoidsIntoPrecategories"}> Coreflection of gropoid objects into pre-category objects
              \.
          %h4#GroupoidObjectDefinition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            with finite
            = succeed "-limits." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          #GroupoidObject.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} groupoid object
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} simplicial object in an (∞,1)-category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X : \Delta^{op} \to \mathcal{C}
            %p satisfying the following equivalent conditions
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
                  satisfies the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      groupoidal
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+conditions"} Segal conditions
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                  and all partitions
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi S
                        %mo ∪
                        %mi S
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n] \simeq S \cup S'
                  that share a single element
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                          %mo ∩
                          %mi S
                          %mo ′
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \cap S' = \{s\}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  exhibits an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi S
                            %mo ∩
                            %mi S
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ;
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        X([n]) \simeq X(S) \times_{X(S \cap S')} X(S')
                        \\,;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
                  is a pre-category object, def.
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PreCategoryObject"}
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Λ
                          %mn 0
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        X(\Delta^2) \to X(\Lambda^2_0)
                %p
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} equivalence
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grpd(\mathcal{C})
              for the
