          %p
            Accordingly, below a
            %em category object
            is defined analogously, but demanding the above condition only for ordered decompositions.
          %p There will be one additional condition on category objects (“completeness”). In order to see where this comes from, notice the following.
          #EmbeddingOfConstantGroupoidObjects.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} full and faithful (∞,1)-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi const
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    const : \mathcal{C} \hookrightarrow Grpd(\mathcal{C})
            %p
              sending an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              to the corresponding constant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi const
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
