          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#ModelCategoryPresentations Model category presentations
          %p
            We discuss here
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentations
            of category objects internal to an
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            theory methods.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+proper+model+category"} left proper
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
              that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presents
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              in that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ≃
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo ∘
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} \simeq C^\circ
            %p
              Then the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects"} simplicial objects
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              admits a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+proper+model+category"} left proper
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
              structure characterized by the following properties:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  it is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
                  of the injective or projective or
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+functors"} model structure on functors
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi op
                          %mo ,
                          %mi C
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mrow
                              %mi proj
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi inj
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi Reedy
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj/inj/Reedy}
              %li
                %p
                  an object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                        %mo →
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^{op} \to C
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+object"} fibrant
                  precisely if it is fibrant in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mrow
                            %mi proj
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi inj
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi Reedy
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj/inj/Reedy}
                  and if the corresponding simplicial object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mo ∘
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^{op}\to C^\circ
                  in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presented
                  by
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  is an internal category.
          %p
            This is stated as (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, prop. 1.5.4
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              By the discussion at
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+functors"} model structure on functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi proj
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi inj
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi Reedy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj/inj/Reedy}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentation
              of
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{op}
              %a{:href => "reflective+sub-%28infinity%2C1%29-category#ModelCategoryPresentation"} reflective sub-(∞,1)-category – model category presentation
              the reflective inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cat
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat_{\mathbf{H}}(\mathcal{C}) \hookrightarrow \mathcal{C}^{\Delta^{op}}
              of cor.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReflectiveInclusionOfCategoryObjectsIntoSimplicialObjects"}
              is presented by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
              as claimed.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = sSet_{Quillen}
              the standard
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+complete+Segal+spaces"} model structure for complete Segal spaces
          %h3#HomotopyTypeTheoryFormulation Homotopy type theory formulation
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            should be to say that we formulate it in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+language"} internal language
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category+in+homotopy+type+theory"} internal category in homotopy type theory
          %p
            However, at the time of this writing little is known for how to speak of
            %em non-finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagrams"} diagrams
            fully internally. To appreciate the issue, notice that the “internal” formulation of categories by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} simplicial objects in an (∞,1)-category
            as
            %a{:href => "#Definition"} above
            is in fact not fully internal to the ambient
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^{op} \to \mathcal{C}
            is. When we speak in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            this is not an option and we have to genuinely stick to internal reasoning.
          %p
            Nevertheless, we can speak fully internally of
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,1)
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                By the discussion at
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-Segal+space"} semi-Segal space
                a category object should equivalently be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-category"} semi-category
                object
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-simplicial+object"} semi-simplicial object
                satisfying the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+conditions"} Segal conditions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Eq
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∂
                            %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Eq(X_1) \hookrightarrow X_1 \stackrel{\partial_1}{\to} X_0
                is an equivalence.
              %p
                A similar formalization of 1-category objects in homotopy type theory has been presented and studied in some detail in (
                %a{:href => "#AKS"}> AKS
                ).
            %li
              %p
                To finite (and “low”) degree a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-simplicial+type"} semi-simplicial type
                may be given “by hand” as a sequence of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+types"} dependent types
                like this:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 0
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                              %mi Type
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 1
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 0
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                              %mi Type
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ;
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ;
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mn 1
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ;
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                              %mi Type
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ⋮
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⊢
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi ⋮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\begin{aligned}
                      \&amp; \vdash\; X_0 \colon Type
                      \\\
                      x_0,x_1 \colon X_0 \;&amp; \vdash \; X_1(x_0,x_1) \colon Type
                      \\\
                      x_0,x_1,x_2 \colon X_1; f_2 \colon X_1(x_0,x_1); f_1 \colon X_1(x_0,x_2); f_2 \colon X_1(x_0,x_1) \;
                      \&amp; \vdash \; X_2(f_0,f_1,f_2) \colon Type
                      \\\
                      \\vdots \; &amp;\vdash\; \vdots
                      \\end{aligned}
              %p
                etc. (Where in principle we can go on like this to any finite
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                at once.)
              %p
                Notice that in the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+types"} dependent types
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+object"} fibrant
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-simplicial+object"} semi-simplicial object
                as used in the standard model-category theoretic constructions of internal
                = succeed "-categories" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#ModelCategoryPresentations"} above
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncated"} n-truncated
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-level"} h-level
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+2
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2C1%29-category"} (n,1)-category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
                should indeed already be determined by its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+skeleton"} simplicial skeleton
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ≤
                            %mo •
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{0 \leq \bullet \leq n+2}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0
                to be
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncated"} n-truncated
                is not sufficient since we also need that
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_2
          %p
            So in conclusion an
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              \-truncated category type
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            should be an
            = succeed "-skeleton" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+2)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-simplicial+type"} semi-simplicial type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≤
                      %mo •
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{0 \leq \bullet \leq 3}
            as above, such that
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+condition"}> Segal condition
                \: for each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi k
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 \leq k \leq n
                the canonical function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 0
                      %mi ⋯
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 0
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n \to X_1 \times_{X_0} \cdots \times_{X_0} X_1
                into the
                = succeed "-fold" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
                is an
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence"}> univalence
                \/unitality: the canonical function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Eq
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∂
                            %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Eq(X_1) \to X_1 \stackrel{\partial_1}{\to} X_0
                is an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            %li
              %p
                truncation: for every
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i
                is
                = succeed "-truncated" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-i)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-level"} h-level
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi i
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-i+2
          %p
            This approach to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2C1%29-categories"} (n,1)-categories
            is discussed in (
            %a{:href => "CapriottiKraus17"}> CapriottiKraus17
            ). There, the last condition is replaced by requiring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
            to be
            = succeed "-truncated," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i
            is
            = succeed "-truncated." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-i)
            %em single
            positive
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "CapriottiKraus17"} CapriottiKraus17
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0
            is
            = succeed "-truncated" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Eq
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Eq(X_1)
            but not
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
            itself.
          %p We spell the above definition out in more detail below for
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
                –
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#0CategoryTypes"} (0,1)-Category types
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i = 1
                for the truncation condition
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
                –
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#1CategoryTypes"} (1,1)-Category types
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i = 2
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_10 Remark
            %p
              %strong (homotopy coherence by dependent types)
            %p
              The formulation of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} simplicial objects in an (∞,1)-category
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+language"} internal language
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
              has to deal with the issue of formulating a simplicial “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+diagram"}> homotopy coherent diagram
              ” in the internal language. One may think of the above formulation via
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimplicial+object"} semisimplicial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+types"} dependent types
              as dealing with this by
            %ol
              %li
                %p discarding the explicit discussion of the degeneracy maps (which are not homotopy-theoretically necessary anyway);
              %li
                %p
                  formulating
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+identities"} simplicial identities
                  %em not
                  as
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+equalities"} propositional equalities
                  (i.e. as
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terms"} terms
                  of some
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mo ∂
                          %mi j
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mo ∂
                          %mi i
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mo ∂
                          %mi j
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mo ∂
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\partial_j \circ\partial_i \simeq \partial_j \circ \partial_{i-1})
                  which would need to be subjected to their own coherent identities) but in fact as typing
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgements"} judgements
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substitution"} substitution
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variables"} variables
                  on which the types of cells
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} depend
            %p
              This is how the above formulation implicitly deals with
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+diagram"} homotopy coherence
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
              this state of affairs translates into the statement that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+object"} fibrant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimplicial+objects"} semisimplicial objects
              are already a good (fibrant+cofibrant) model for
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
          %h4#HCategoryTypes H-Category types
          %p
            It may be instructive to begin by discussing a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal category
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            which is
            %em not
            an category object in an
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %em not
            interpret as an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-category"} H-category
            that underlies in particular any genuine precategory object, by def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyCategoryOfPreCategoryObject"}
            above.
          %p Notice that historically one says that:
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_14 Definition
            %p
              An
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-monoid"} H-monoid
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+object"} monoid object
              internal to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28%E2%88%9EGrpd%29"} Ho(∞Grpd)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28Top%29"} Ho(Top)
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_11 Remark
            %p
              This means that an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-monoid"} H-monoid
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p
                  equipped with a binary operation
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdot \colon X \times X \to X
              %li
                %p
                  and equipped with a point
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo *
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon * \to X
            %p such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  there
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantifier"} exists
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associativity
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo )
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mo )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mo )
                            %mo )
                          %mo )
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mo )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mo )
                            %mo )
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo )
                          %mo )
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\left(\left(-\right) \cdot \left(\left(-\right) \cdot \left(-\right)\right)\right)
                        \\Rightarrow
                        \\left(\left(\left(-\right) \cdot \left(-\right)\right) \cdot \left(-\right)\right)
                        \\colon
                        X \times X \times X \to X
              %li
                %p
                  there exists a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+law"} unitality
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi id
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (i \cdot (-)) \to id \colon  X \to X
                        \\,.
            %p
              The point here is that these homotopies are only required to exist, but are not specified and are not part of the data of an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-monoid"} H-monoid
          %p
            One also speaks of an
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-group"} H-group
            for an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-monoid"} H-monoid
            for which the product operation similarly has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverses"} inverses
            up to unspecified homotopies. Hence it makes sense to consider the following many-object version (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oidification"}> oidification
            ”) of this classical concept:
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_15 Definition
            %p
              An
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-category"} H-category
                type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊢
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vdash \; X_0  \colon
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Type"} Type
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} dependent type
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⊢
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi Type
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0,x_1 \colon X_0 \;\vdash\; X_1(x_0,x_1) \colon Type
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term"} term
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi i
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vdash \; i \colon X_0
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⊢
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi comp
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mn 2
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        x_0,x_1,x_2 \colon X_0 \;\vdash\; comp_{x_1,x_2,x_2} \colon X_1(x_0,x_1) \times X_1(x_1,x_2) \to X_1(x_0,x_2)
            %p
              such that there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term"} term
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi com
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 3
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi comp
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi comp
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi comp
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x_0, x_1, x_2, x_3 \colon X_0 \;\vdash\; ( com_{x_0,x_2,x_3} \circ comp_{x_0,x_1,x_2} \simeq  comp_{x_0, x_1, x_2} \circ comp_{x_1,x_2,x_3})
            %p
              (hence, equivalently, a necessarily unique term of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
              = succeed "(\u2026)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+type"} isInhabited
          %p
            The archetypical example of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-groups"} H-groups
            already illustrates the deficiency of this notion
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \colon * \to Y
              a pointed
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"} loop space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi y
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_y Y
              is naturally equipped with the structure of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-group"} H-group
              by
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  taking the unit
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi y
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} * \to \Omega_y Y
                  to be the constant loop on
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %li
                %p taking the product to be given by any choice of concatenation of loops.
          %p
            The natural question arising then is: how are those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-groups"} H-groups
            characterized that arise as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+objects"} loop space objects
          %p
            One observes that those that areise this way carry much more structure than just a composition and unit up to unspecified homotopy: we can instead make an explicit choice of such homotopies by choosing ways to reparameterize the interval and, crucially, any two such choices are themselves related by a choice of higher order homotopy, and so ever on. Such a structure is called a
            %strong strong homotopy monoid
            structure with
            %strong strong homotopy associativity
            (as opposed to just bare homotopy associativity as in an
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-monoid"} H-monoid
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} A-∞
            structure.
          %p
            The classical result by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
            answered the question by saying that:
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-group"} H-group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \cdot)
              arises as a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \simeq \Omega Y
              precisely if its homotopy-monoidal structure may be lifted to an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} A-∞ algebra
              structure.
          %p
            The point of the following constructions is to take care of that additional
            %em strong
            homotopy information.
